        "note": "$1,800 per child under 18 for 2026 (indexed from 2026, it was $1,750), refundable, no cap. It is combined with the working family credit, 4% of the first $9,690 of earned income, and \"the combined amount of the credits is reduced by 12 percent of earned income or adjusted gross income, whichever is greater, in excess of the phaseout threshold\": $38,770 joint, $32,680 for everyone else. earnedIncomeAddOn is the working family credit for a filer with a child. Earned income is used as the basis, since wages are never below AGI for the calculator's inputs. Left out: the working family credit for filers with no child under 18, the extra $1,020 to $2,770 for children 18 or older, the investment income limit, and advance payments.",
